level_guide_text = "[center][b][u]LEVEL 3: ARRAYS (LISTS)[/u][/b][/center]

[b]OBJECTIVE:[/b]
Variables can hold lists! Match the [color=yellow]comma-separated lists[/color] to the correct Array container.

[b]THEORY GUIDE:[/b]

[b]1. INTEGER ARRAY (int[])[/b]
A list of whole numbers inside curly brackets.
[i]Example:[/i] [code]int[] scores = {10, 20, 30};[/code]

[b]2. STRING ARRAY (String[])[/b]
A list of words inside quotes.
[i]Example:[/i] [code]String[] fruits = {\"Apple\", \"Banana\"};[/code]

[b]3. CHARACTER ARRAY (char[])[/b]
A list of single letters inside single quotes.
[i]Example:[/i] [code]char[] grades = {'X', 'Y', 'Z'};[/code]"

